DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't try to catch the falling AI names.</b> The biggest AI and chip stocks have lost about $5 trillion since early October while most other stocks rose; keep regular investing (DCA) in broad funds instead of loading up on one fallen name.",
"<b>Spread your risk beyond tech.</b> Nine of 11 S&P sectors rose last week even as the index fell; a broad or equal-weight fund keeps you from leaning too hard on AI.",
"<b>Expect a bumpy week.</b> Apple tonight, the midterms Tuesday, possible Iran strikes after the vote and the jobs report Friday can all move prices; don't trade on one headline.",
"<b>Rates are still high.</b> A December hike is still about 70% likely; avoid new high-interest debt and lock in fixed rates where you can. Cash and short-term bonds still pay while you wait.",
"<b>Budget for higher fuel.</b> Oil eased to about $102 but rose more than 10% in October, and Hormuz is still effectively shut; US diesel is about $6.30.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a bet.</b> It bounced to about $3,900 from a one-year low; if you hold some, keep it a small slice and don't chase either way.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> Binance saw about $3.6B leave after it reopened withdrawals; don't keep more on an exchange than you need.",
"<b>Thai investors: be patient and selective.</b> The SET (1,518.59) sits just above 1,500-1,515 support after a 2.82% weekly drop. In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, AP, TVO and PTT trade at or below their buy zones (green); check earnings and payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 26.2 = Fear, near the Extreme Fear line (unchanged since Friday's close, as US stocks have not traded), down from 34.6 after the tech selloff. Momentum and safe-haven demand are in extreme fear."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~46 = Elevated, up 1: Trump says he is in 'no hurry' and still has targets in Iran, Khamenei ordered an unrestricted response plan, more tankers were hit, and the Oleshky truce ended. Talks via Qatar continue."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 14.6 = extreme fear: Friday's 1.8% drop pushed the index below its 100-day average."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 32.4 = fear (92 NYSE highs vs 169 lows Friday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 37.2 = fear, though most sectors still rose last week: the selling was concentrated in AI and chips."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 27.8 = lots of protection buying, a fearful sign."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 26.5 = fear: the VIX is about 19.4, after touching its highest intraday level since April on Friday."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 2.2 = extreme fear: bonds have beaten stocks as money hid from tech."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 43.0 = fear, slipping from neutral: lenders are getting a bit more careful."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 67 (up from 66): Trump says he is in 'no hurry' and still has 'one or two sites' to hit, and Khamenei ordered an unrestricted response plan, though talks via Qatar continue. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 38 (up from 37), the biggest weight: the Oleshky truce ended without extension and Russia hit energy in four regions, while three-way talks are being prepared."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 75 (up from 74): at least four tankers were hit Fri-Sat, including one deep in the Gulf, and a Qatari LNG tanker with safe passage was struck."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 20 (unchanged): a third day of Iran-Qatar talks in Doha, and Rubio says the US wants to broker a Ukraine deal."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 25 (unchanged): no explicit nuclear threats; the Qatar plan would restart talks on Iran's nuclear program."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,580 Friday (−1.82%), its worst day since June; futures are about 0.3% higher early Monday."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −1.09% Friday; futures about +0.2%."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −2.86% Friday as Intel crashed 29% and chips sold off; the Nasdaq 100 briefly hit correction territory. Futures about +0.4%."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.93% Friday: below 5% as investors bought bonds for safety."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$102.4 early Monday (−1.6%) after OPEC+ held output steady, down from Friday's $104.12, the highest close since mid-September."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$111.6 for the January contract (−1.5%); the expired December contract settled at $117.64 Friday."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.30/gal (AAA, 1 Nov), just under the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,900 early Monday (+0.6%), bouncing from Friday's one-year low, as higher oil kept Fed hike bets alive; $4,000 is now resistance."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$78.3k = still bearish but steadier, even as about $3.6B left Binance after it reopened withdrawals."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct with two officials wanting a hike; next decision 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal; the Fed's preferred PCE gauge was 3.6% in September."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 70.7% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec, slipping from about 76% earlier in the week."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. About 102.0, little changed early Monday."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~157.5 = a weak yen; the BOJ held at 1.25% on Friday but said its 2% inflation goal is met, which points to more hikes."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT raised its 2026 growth forecast to 2.4%, sees inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,518.59 Fri 30 Oct, −2.82% for the week after touching 1,511.58, a 5½-month low; KS sees support at 1,515 and 1,500 and resistance at 1,530 and 1,550 this week."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿1.06B on 30 Oct, ending two days of selling; October about −฿6.6B and year to date about +฿18.5B (our sums of SET data)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
