DASH.glossary.hl={m:"Breadth",d:"New highs = NYSE stocks at a 52-week high; new lows = at a 52-week low. Index up while lows outnumber highs = a narrow bounce. Latest session (Fri 30 Oct, still the latest before Monday's US open): 92 highs vs 169 lows (WSJ). Both rose from 62 vs 120, but lows grew more as the S&P fell 1.8%. Still, 9 of 11 S&P sectors rose last week, so the damage is concentrated in AI and chips. Watch whether lows keep climbing this week."};
